// Commonwealth Order of Battle. Every id validated against
// data/reference/unit-characteristics/commonwealth.ron (see ob_ids_are_valid_characteristics_keys).
//
// CHART-VERIFIED (D14 retired for these formations, 2026-08-30): both loaded formations were checked
// against the §4.44a Commonwealth OA sheets (transcribed from the rulebook PDF to
// docs/source-materials/cw-ob-4.44a.transcribed.md). 4th Indian Division (PDF p126) matches
// exactly — HQs "a", rifle battalions "p", Central India Horse "ll", field artillery "x", weapons
// and arrivals all confirmed. 7th Armoured Division matches its OA sheet exactly (HQs b/b/d, tanks
// "g", motor infantry "n", RHA "aa"/"x", 11th Hussars "ll"). No id corrections were required.
//
// The remaining §4.44a formations (PDF p118–132) were promoted from that transcription on
// 2026-08-30. id codes are copied verbatim from the chart-verified transcription; every weapon
// system name maps to the exact §4.47 key in data/reference/weapons/commonwealth.ron. Arrivals
// use the transcription's stage/game-turn convention ("n/mm" = Operations Stage n, Game-Turn mm).
// Notes on non-obvious decisions:
//   * 13th DCO Lancers in the 18th Indian Brigade prints a BLANK id cell on that chart; the
//     transcription's own note cross-references the identical unit on the Unassigned Indian sheet
//     where it is "ll", so id "ll" is used here (documented value, not a guess).
//   * 1st Regt d'artillerie (1st Free French Bde) is armed with "French 149mm" guns, which have no
//     key in the Commonwealth §4.47 chart — modeled as Organic(Normal) on its "y" artillery id.
(
    formations: [
